---
/* About ATLStay.
 *
 * The story here is the OWNER'S, supplied 2026-09-01, not invented: four people
 * who did every job themselves, then built departments around what they had
 * learned. Keep it that way — this is the page where an owner decides whether
 * to trust us with an asset, and a fabricated detail here would poison the
 * whole site.
 *
 * TWO CLAIMS FROM THE SOURCE MATERIAL ARE DELIBERATELY NOT PUBLISHED:
 *   1. "#1-rated property manager in the eastern United States" — a superlative
 *      ranking with no attributable source. Unverifiable superlatives are an
 *      advertising risk and are exactly what E-E-A-T assessment penalises.
 *      Restore it only alongside the award or ranking body that issued it.
 *   2. "across the United States" — the whole site, its schema and its ranking
 *      strategy are metro-Atlanta and Georgia. A national claim would contradict
 *      every location page and weaken the local relevance that is working.
 * Both were raised with the owner rather than quietly dropped.
 *
 * The service list is deliberately SHORT and linked rather than described. The
 * source material described all sixteen service lines at length; reproducing
 * that here would have duplicated the service pages themselves, which is the
 * exact defect that was measured and fixed across the 454 city pages.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '@/components/ui/Section.astro';
import Container from '@/components/ui/Container.astro';
import Eyebrow from '@/components/ui/Eyebrow.astro';
import Card from '@/components/ui/Card.astro';
import CTABand from '@/components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import ServiceFormBand from '@/components/services/ServiceFormBand.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
import { images } from '@/data/images';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '@/lib/schema';
import { serviceLines } from '@/data/serviceLines';

const schemas = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
  ]),
];

/* The jobs the founders did themselves before any of them was a department.
   This is the credibility of the whole page: it is specific, and nobody who
   had not done the work would list these. */
const didItOurselves = [
  'Answered guest messages',
  'Coordinated cleaners',
  'Took the maintenance calls',
  'Worked with tenants',
  'Spoke to owners directly',
  'Got homes ready for market',
  'Built and rewrote listings',
  'Chased contractors',
  'Handled the emergencies',
  'Adjusted the pricing',
  'Ran the turnovers',
  'Fixed what went wrong',
];

/* Each became a function once the portfolio outgrew four people doing all of
   it. Ordered roughly the way an owner encounters them. */
const operations = [
  { name: 'Property onboarding', line: 'Condition, positioning and readiness before anything goes live.' },
  { name: 'Revenue management', line: 'Pricing that moves with demand instead of sitting still for months.' },
  { name: 'Leasing', line: 'Marketing, showings, screening and execution for longer-term tenancies.' },
  { name: 'Guest services', line: 'Round-the-clock communication, because arrivals do not keep office hours.' },
  { name: 'Cleaning', line: 'Turnovers to a set standard, inspected rather than assumed.' },
  { name: 'Maintenance', line: 'Coordination and a vendor network, not a list of numbers handed to you.' },
  { name: 'Owner relations', line: 'One point of contact who knows your property.' },
  { name: 'Accounting & reporting', line: 'Statements you can read without decoding them.' },
];

/* Why owners actually leave their previous manager. Owner-supplied. */
const whyOwnersMove = [
  'Communication went quiet',
  'Maintenance only ever reactive',
  'The property underperforming',
  'Pricing untouched for months',
  'Cleaning quality drifting',
  'Vacancies running long',
  'Nobody reachable after hours',
  'Outgrew a manager who could not scale',
  'Tired of managing the manager',
];

const values = [
  {
    title: 'The property decides the strategy',
    text: 'Not every home should be an Airbnb. Not every home should have a twelve-month tenant. The right answer depends on the asset, the location, the regulations and what you actually want from it — not on whichever service earns us the most.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Own the problem until it is solved',
    text: 'Not "that is the cleaner\'s responsibility". Not "call the contractor". Not "contact the platform". You hired a management company so you would not have to be the coordinator between six different people. That is the job.',
  },
  {
    title: 'One clear fee',
    text: `Short-term and furnished management is ${site.pricing.rate} of booking revenue, all-inclusive. Long-term, commercial and community management is quoted per property or per door. You see the rate before you sign anything.`,
  },
  {
    title: 'Technology where it helps, people where they matter',
    text: 'Pricing systems, channel sync, digital reporting — all necessary. But software cannot inspect a property, notice a turnover fell short, or reassure a frustrated tenant. We use technology to make people faster, not to remove them.',
  },
  {
    title: 'We say no',
    text: 'We do not take every property that comes to us. We run a real projection and have an honest conversation first. If a home is not going to perform, telling you that is more useful than signing you.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Local decisions, locally made',
    text: `We are based in ${site.contact.address.city}, and we know why a Buckhead corporate stay prices differently from a BeltLine weekend because we work here — not because we read it in a report.`,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ATLStay — From Four People to a Full Property Operation"
  description={`ATLStay began with four people who did every job themselves. Today it is a full property management operation across metro Atlanta — short-term, long-term, furnished, commercial and community. Based in ${site.contact.address.city}, GA.`}
  image={images.about.src}
  schemas={schemas}
>

  <PageHero
    title="Four people. One idea. A different standard for property management."
    subtitle="ATLStay did not start with departments, technology or a 24/7 operations centre. It started with four people who thought owners should not have to choose between a local team that cares and a national company that has the infrastructure."
    eyebrow="OUR STORY"
    imageKey="about"
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
    cta={{ label: 'Get my free rental projection', href: '/rental-projection/' }}
  />

  <!-- ─── THE CHOICE NOBODY SHOULD HAVE TO MAKE ─── -->
  <Section variant="white">
    <Container>
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center lg:gap-20">
        <div>
          <Eyebrow>Why we started</Eyebrow>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
            Owners were being asked to pick a side.
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-ink/75">
            <p>
              Hire a small local manager and you get personal attention with limited
              resources. Hire a national company and you get real infrastructure —
              and become one address inside an enormous portfolio.
            </p>
            <p>
              We did not think that was a fair choice. So we set out to build the
              infrastructure of a national property management company with the
              accountability of a local team.
            </p>
            <p class="font-medium text-forest">That idea became {site.brandName}.</p>
            <p>
              What started with four people now runs as an organisation with
              dedicated teams across every part of the rental lifecycle. But what
              it became only makes sense once you know how it began.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-forest-50">
            <img src={images.about.src} alt={images.about.alt} loading="lazy" class="h-full w-full object-cover" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── BEFORE THERE WERE DEPARTMENTS ─── -->
  <Section variant="cream">
    <Container>
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <Eyebrow>How it started</Eyebrow>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
          Before there were departments, we did it ourselves.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-ink/75">
          There was no guest services team. No leasing team. No revenue desk, no
          maintenance division, no vendor network. There were properties that had
          to perform, and four people determined to make that happen.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="mx-auto mt-10 grid max-w-4xl gap-x-8 gap-y-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {didItOurselves.map((job) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-[15px] text-ink/80">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-none rounded-full bg-brass"></span>
            {job}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-brass/60 bg-white/70 p-7 sm:p-9">
        <p class="text-ink/80">
          When something went wrong there was no other department to hand it to.
          We had to solve it. That is where the standard came from — and it is why
          we still believe great property management is not one big thing. It is
          hundreds of small things done correctly, consistently, and usually before
          an owner knows they needed doing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── BUILDING THE ORGANISATION ─── -->
  <Section variant="white">
    <Container>
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <Eyebrow>How it grew</Eyebrow>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
          We did not just grow a portfolio. We built an operation.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-ink/75">
          As more owners trusted us there was a decision to make: keep piling
          properties onto individual managers until everyone was overwhelmed, or
          build the infrastructure properly. We built the infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {operations.map((op) => (
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6">
            <h3 class="font-display text-base text-forest">{op.name}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">{op.line}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-center text-ink/75">
        Behind those functions sit property managers, leasing professionals, guest
        support, cleaners, maintenance technicians, revenue specialists, licensed
        real estate professionals and an extensive contractor network. Support runs
        around the clock, because a guest can be locked out at midnight and an air
        conditioner does not care that it is Sunday.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── MORE THAN AIRBNB ─── -->
  <Section variant="tint">
    <Container>
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <Eyebrow>What we do now</Eyebrow>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
          Short-term rentals were the beginning. They are not the whole story.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-ink/75">
          <p>
            As our owners' portfolios grew, what they needed changed. Some wanted
            nightly income, others wanted a twelve-month tenant. Some needed
            furnished housing for corporate stays, healthcare contracts or insurance
            placements. Some bought multifamily. Some bought commercial. Investors
            started asking us to look at properties <em>before</em> they bought them.
          </p>
          <p>
            What almost none of them wanted was five different companies handling
            five different parts of one portfolio. They wanted one organisation that
            could do the lot. So we built one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
        {serviceLines.map((s) => (
          <a
            href={`/services/${s.slug}/`}
            class="rounded-full border border-line bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm text-ink/80 transition-colors hover:border-brass hover:bg-white hover:text-forest focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-forest"
          >{s.name}</a>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-ink/75">
        The important part is not the length of that list. It is that the same team
        can move a property between strategies when the market, the regulations or
        your plans change — without you rebuilding your whole team to do it.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── HOW WE OPERATE ─── -->
  <Section variant="white">
    <Container>
      <div class="text-center">
        <Eyebrow>How we operate</Eyebrow>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
          The principles behind every decision.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {values.map((v) => (
          <Card>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg text-forest">{v.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/75">{v.text}</p>
          </Card>
        ))}
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <ServiceFormBand variant="tint" />

  <!-- ─── WHY OWNERS COME TO US ─── -->
  <Section variant="cream">
    <Container>
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
        <div>
          <Eyebrow>Why owners move</Eyebrow>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
            Nobody looks for a new manager when everything is going well.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-ink/75">
            Owners come to us because something stopped working. Usually one of these:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-2.5 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {whyOwnersMove.map((r) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2.5 text-[15px] text-ink/80">
                <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-none rounded-full bg-brass"></span>
                {r}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-forest">What happens after you hand us the keys</h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink/75">
            You are not hiring one person with a phone. Your property gets assessed
            for condition, positioning, pricing, photography, compliance and
            readiness — then the right teams take it on.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink/75">
            Revenue specialists work the revenue. Leasing works the leasing. Cleaners
            hold the presentation standard. Maintenance keeps it operating. Guest
            support handles guests. Specialists where specialisation matters, one
            organisation accountable for the result — and you can see what is
            happening throughout.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-5">
            <a href="/how-it-works/" class="font-medium text-forest underline decoration-brass/60 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-brass-600">
              See the full onboarding process
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── FACTS ─── -->
  <!-- NAMED BIOS ARE A SETTLED "NO", not an outstanding to-do. The owner
       decided on 2026-09-01 not to publish team names, on the reasoning that
       large firms generally don't either. Do not keep asking for them, and do
       not invent people to fill the gap — this section carries verified company
       facts instead, which is the honest way to build the same trust. -->
  <Section variant="white">
    <Container>
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <Eyebrow>The team</Eyebrow>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest sm:text-4xl">
          Big enough to deliver. Close enough to care.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-ink/75">
          There are advantages to being small and advantages to being large, and we
          built {site.brandName} to hold on to both. However big the portfolio gets,
          every property still belongs to somebody — it is capital, income, often the
          largest thing a family owns. Scale is never a reason to forget that.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-11 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-7 text-center">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl text-forest">{site.stats.years}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/70">years managing property in Georgia, since {site.stats.foundingYear}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-7 text-center">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl text-forest">Licensed</p>
          <!-- Deliberately attributed to the TEAM, not to a named legal entity.
               The group runs several companies and sister companies, and stating
               that one specific entity holds the brokerage licence is a claim we
               should not be on the hook for. "Licensed professionals on our team"
               is true regardless of which entity holds what. Do not reintroduce a
               company name here. -->
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/70">Licensed Georgia real estate professionals on our team — so we can handle leasing, long-term rentals and community management, not just hosting</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-7 text-center">
          <p class="font-display text-3xl text-forest">{site.stats.homes}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink/70">homes and communities under management</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-7 max-w-2xl text-center text-sm text-ink/70">
        Based in {site.contact.address.city}, {site.contact.address.region} — {site.contact.address.street},
        in Buckhead. Reach us on <a href={site.contact.phoneHref} class="font-medium text-forest underline decoration-brass/60 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brass-600">{site.contact.phone}</a>
        or <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="font-medium text-forest underline decoration-brass/60 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brass-600">{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── SCALE ─── -->
  <Section variant="forest">
    <Container>
      <div class="text-center">
        <Eyebrow class="text-brass">Track record</Eyebrow>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-cream sm:text-4xl">
          More capable was always the point. Not bigger.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/5 p-8 text-center ring-1 ring-white/10">
          <p class="font-display text-2xl text-brass">{site.scale.portfolioPhrase}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream/65">trusted to us by Georgia owners</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/5 p-8 text-center ring-1 ring-white/10">
          <p class="font-display text-2xl text-brass">{site.scale.staysPhrase}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream/65">five-star guest experiences</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/5 p-8 text-center ring-1 ring-white/10">
          <p class="font-display text-2xl text-brass">{site.scale.bookingsPhrase}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream/65">in revenue managed for owners</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-2xl text-center text-cream/70">
        More people available when something goes wrong. More expertise around the
        investment. More ways to generate demand, more systems protecting the
        property, and more options when the market shifts. That is what the growth
        was for.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Let's talk about your property."
    text="Get a free projection and find out whether we're the right fit for your home."
  />

</BaseLayout>
